WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.588
This lesson uses three evidence layers.

2
00:00:02.588 --> 00:00:09.954
First, the current CVA6 repository documentation is the authority for what C V, A and six mean in this project.

3
00:00:09.954 --> 00:00:18.448
Second, the current User Manual tells us what a named configuration actually implements and whether a name is still provisional.

4
00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:26.875
Third, an older public CORE-V deck explains the historical five-field syntax behind names such as C V thirty two E four zero P.

5
00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:32.250
That history is valuable, but current documentation wins whenever the two differ.

